{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfTg8bPvNaPRBEJ8b3z1W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add a new ErrorCode enum value `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to represent the error when trying to confirm a CANCELLED shipment. This maintains the convention that each conflict scenario has its own error code.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`:\n   - Receives a `shipmentId` path variable\n   - Retrieves the shipment from the repository\n   - Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) if shipment doesn't exist\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throws `ConflictException` (409) with `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` code\n   - If status is `CONFIRMED`, returns the shipment unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If status is `CREATED`, updates it to `CONFIRMED` and saves it\n   - Returns the shipment in all success cases (200)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test cases covering:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED and returns it\n   - Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and returns it unchanged\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM error code\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n**Alternative approaches rejected:**\n\n1. **Add a service/business logic layer** — The existing code doesn't have a service layer; all logic is in the controller. Adding one would violate the \"preserve existing architecture\" constraint.\n\n2. **Use SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS for cancelled conflict** — This would be misleading; the shipment exists but is in the wrong state, not that it's a duplicate.\n\n3. **Idempotent via HTTP GET instead of POST** — The requirement explicitly asks for `POST`, which is correct since this is a state transition action, not just a read.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Validation | Write | Response | Status |\n|------|------|-----------|-------|----------|--------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | findById(id) | status==CREATED | save(copy with CONFIRMED) | Shipment | 200 |\n| CONFIRMED (retry) | findById(id) | status==CONFIRMED | none | Shipment | 200 |\n| CANCELLED | findById(id) | status==CANCELLED | none | error | 409 |\n| Not found | findById(id) returns null | - | none | error | 404 |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `confirms a CREATED shipment` — Create shipment S-1, confirm it, verify status is CONFIRMED\n2. `confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds` — Confirm twice, both succeed, status stays CONFIRMED  \n3. `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment` — Write CANCELLED shipment directly to repo, try to confirm, expect 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n4. `reports an unknown shipment` — Try to confirm non-existent shipment S-missing, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_read_input_tokens":17694,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":819},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9634937-b1c9-4f46-9a83-f5387b675913","uuid":"0db57698-73d0-42f3-9faf-45316883835f","timestamp":"2026-09-27T09:04:13.010Z","request_id":"req_011CfTg8b2qyZnrZbYjTevB5"}
